rce":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 30 - The Sweet Sound of 70s Bubblegum Music","url":"https://seventies.libsyn.com/030-bubblegum"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Saturday Morning Cartoon (1972)","body":"The Osmonds received their own Saturday morning cartoon in 1972, which featured their 1970 number one hit \"One Bad Apple\" as its theme song. \"They even got their own Saturday morning cartoon in 1972 And the theme song was their 1970 number one hit one bad apple.\"","year":1972,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 27 - That's Entertainment! TV Variety Shows of the 70s","url":null},{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 27 - That's Entertainment! TV Variety Shows of the 70s","url":"https://seventies.libsyn.com/027-variety-shows-12920-5-16-pm"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"American Music Association Best Country Group or Duo Award (1976)","body":"In 1976, The Osmonds were awarded the American Music Association Best Country Group or Duo Award, reflecting the blurry lines between country and pop genres in the 1970s. \"They won the American Music Association Best Country Group or Duo Award in 1976 Country? Yeah, I guess so again, the line between Country and Pop was so blurry in the 70s, so I can see it.\"","year":1976,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 27 - That's Entertainment! TV Variety Shows of the 70s","url":null},{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 27 - That's Entertainment! TV Variety Shows of the 70s","url":"https://seventies.libsyn.com/027-variety-shows-12920-5-16-pm"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Early Career on The Andy Williams Show (1960s)","body":"In the 1960s, The Osmonds frequently appeared on \"The Andy Williams Show,\" a \"classic 60s variety show\" known for being \"very family friendly,\" which often featured acts like Dick Van Dyke or The New Christy Minstrels. \"In the 60s the Osmonds were likely to be found on the Andy Williams show The classic 60s variety show that was definitely very quote family friendly.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 27 - That's Entertainment! TV Variety Shows of the 70s","url":null},{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 27 - That's Entertainment! TV Variety Shows of the 70s","url":"https://seventies.libsyn.com/027-variety-shows-12920-5-16-pm"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Image Reinvention and Creative Control","body":"By 1973, with Donnie as a teen heartthrob, the Osmonds sought to shed their \"Andy Williams image.\" They signed with a new record label, which granted them greater creative control over their careers. \"But he and his brothers had to get rid of that Andy Williams image They got a new record label and along with that they got a bit more control Over the creative direction of their careers.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 27 - That's Entertainment! TV Variety Shows of the 70s","url":null},{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 27 - That's Entertainment! TV Variety Shows of the 70s","url":"https://seventies.libsyn.com/027-variety-shows-12920-5-16-pm"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Pop Group Comparison","body":"Critic Charlie Gillette suggested that Dr. Hook, if they were to \"relax and become a straight pop group,\" could \"wipe the Osmonds and the Partridge Family off the board,\" indicating The Osmonds' status as a popular, clean-cut pop group at the time. \"They would wipe the osmonds and the partridge family off the board.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 44 - Streaking, Werewolves, Sharks, & Drinking - 70s Novelty Songs","url":null},{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 44 - Streaking, Werewolves, Sharks, & Drinking - 70s Novelty Songs","url":"https://traffic.libsyn.com/seventies/334334714-44100-2-e5ed6adac25ea.m4a"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Recording at FAME Studios, Muscle Shoals, AL","body":"The Osmonds recorded \"One Bad Apple\" at the legendary FAME Studios in Muscle Shoals, Alabama, a studio famed for hosting iconic R&B and soul artists like Aretha Franklin, Wilson Pickett, The Rolling Stones, and Etta James. \"I mean this is what the studio where Aretha Franklin and Wilson pick it And the Rolling Stones and edit James and acts like that recorded I mean the Osmonds recorded at Muscle Shoals? Yes they did.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 27 - That's Entertainment! TV Variety Shows of the 70s","url":null},{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 27 - That's Entertainment! TV Variety Shows of the 70s","url":"https://seventies.libsyn.com/027-variety-shows-12920-5-16-pm"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Rejection of Bubblegum Label","body":"The Osmonds themselves did not like being labeled as a bubblegum band; they aspired to be recognized as a rock act. \"Now the Osmonds may not have liked the bubble gum label they didn't. They wanted to be considered rock.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 30 - The Sweet Sound of 70s Bubblegum Music","url":null},{"source":"For the Record - The 70s","episode":"Ep. 30 - The Sweet Sound of 70s Bubblegum Music","url":"https://seventies.libsyn.com/030-bubblegum"}]}],"awards":[{"kind":"award","title":"star on Hollywood Walk of Fame (2003)","body":"Won.","year":2003,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q17985761"}]}],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":20847420674594,"type":"song","name":"One Bad Apple","work_year":1971,"list_id":219509302503571,"list":"Billboard Hot 100 nº1 · 1970s","src":"singles","rank":249,"year":1971,"note":"5 semanas","yt":"S7pGsnd41XQ","scaruffi":null},{"id":20847420674594,"type":"song","name":"One Bad Apple","work_year":1971,"list_id":114443832640485,"list":"Billboard Year-End 1